# Long, safe cache lifetimes for genuinely static binary assets that never
# change without a deliberate edit-and-redeploy — board textures and the PWA
# install icons. 30 days, not a full year: these have no cache-busting hash
# in their filenames, so a browser or edge cache that held one for a full
# year would keep serving it after a real update. 30 days bounds that risk
# to something a maintainer would actually notice, while still comfortably
# clearing the threshold Lighthouse's "efficient cache lifetimes" audit
# checks for.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to script.js, style.css, data.js, sw.js,
# index.html, or manifest.json — those change on every feature, and this
# project already spent real debugging time on exactly the bug a long cache
# on those would reintroduce (see the README's caching-bug history). They
# keep Cloudflare's default `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` with an
# ETag: always re-checked, never blindly held past its actual staleness.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, must-revalidate

/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, must-revalidate
